  by: agent  # 605e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 605e
  clock: 4  # 605e
  nonce: 605e  # 605e
  message: "Fixed via merged PR (dev b4159608dc). Labeling/disclosure fix per the ruling — no value change. Recharacterization: the field was renamed (centrality_scores -> additional_file_centrality_scores) and recomputed (Σ in-degree of mentioned symbols ÷ file length in chars, ranking.py:1652) by the WI-rajod/WI-ribag rework AFTER this item was filed, but the misleading 'centrality'/'normalized' label survived. Behavioral anchor (new characterization test test_score_is_indegree_density_not_zero_to_one_normalized): a 3-char file naming an in-degree-30 symbol scores 10.0 — an order of magnitude outside [0,1], proving it is an unbounded density, not a normalized centrality. Relabel: docs/schema.json additional_file_centrality_scores description now states the exact formula + that the score is unbounded >=0, repo-relative, and a ranking key only (NOT a probability/[0,1] centrality); the cli producer comment and CentralityResult.normalized_scores docstring carry the same disclosure (field name documented as historical: normalized by file size, not range). The characterization test fails if anyone re-normalizes to [0,1] without updating the label. 100% cov; targeted manifest (80 tests incl. test_ranking)."  # 605e
